      "diagnosis": "The naturalsize() function has rounding issues where values that should round up to 1000/1024 at one suffix level don't properly carry over to the next suffix level. For example, a value that computes to 999.9+ and rounds to 1000.0 should use the next higher suffix instead of staying at the current one.",
      "hypothesis": "The issue occurs because after computing the formatted value using the format string, we don't check if the formatted result rounds to the next threshold (1000 for decimal, 1024 for binary). We need to detect when rounding causes the mantissa to reach the next unit boundary and adjust accordingly.",
